<rss version="0.92"><channel><item>
            <title>[LU-20629] fallocate restart resumes at a block count used as a byte offset</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20629</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;osd_fallocate_preallocate() advances the caller's byte offset *start by the block count from ldiskfs_map_blocks() ("*start += rc;", osd_io.c). *start is ofd_object_fallocate()'s resume point across its -EAGAIN restart loop, so a restart resumes ~4096x too early and re-maps what it already mapped.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Found by graph-hunter-v1&lt;/p&gt;</description>
